@display("std/project")
project: part {
  | The implementation side of a spec that lives apart from its code: the declaration that a
  | tree implements a spec at a version, the proofs that link the spec's requirements to the
  | tests that prove them at a [revision](#heron.language.specifications.layers.revisions.revision), where the rest stands, the releases, the
  | implementation's own components, and its delivery: `story`, `increment` and `milestone` nodes.
  |
  | Its surface is declared in `std/project/package.heron`, whose types the API reference renders.
  | `implements` and `release` are specified in [Specs and implementations](#language.specifications.implementations), `proves`, `verify`, `status`, `<planned>` and `<untested>` in [Proof, revisions and gaps](#language.specifications.traceability), and the components and delivery kinds in [Delivery](#language.specifications.delivery).
}
